
# 🔬 Research Council Context Comparison 20260616 — integrate-system-scribe-latency-20260616T050042Z
**Author:** Scribe
**Version:** v0.1
**Status:** in_progress
**Last Updated:** 2026-06-16 05:06:17 UTC

> Wave 1 Track D comparison of Scribe MCP invocation/config surfaces in scribe_mcp versus council_mcp.

---
## Executive Summary
<!-- ID: executive_summary -->
Track D found no evidence that `scribe_mcp` and `council_mcp` currently register different Scribe MCP servers for Claude/Codex clients. Both current generated configs point `scribe` at `/home/austin/miniconda3/envs/uap/bin/scribe-server` with `SCRIBE_ROOT=/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp`, `SCRIBE_MODE=server`, and `SCRIBE_STORAGE_BACKEND=postgres` (`scribe_mcp/.mcp.json:13-19`, `scribe_mcp/.codex/config.toml:119-123`, `council_mcp/.mcp.json:13-19`, `council_mcp/.codex/config.toml:124-128`). Council MCP source confirms this is intentional: exported Scribe configs target the Scribe runtime checkout, and workspace binding is delegated to `set_project` (`council_mcp/src/council_mcp/services/scribe_launch.py:49-77`, `:109-146`).

The stronger evidence-backed latency hypotheses are therefore not "different Scribe server" hypotheses. They are:
1. `set_project(root=/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/council_mcp)` exercises different Scribe internal work than the `scribe_mcp` root: repo-root authorization, alias lookup, path validation, document scaffold checks, dev-plan upserts, existing-project inventory, and reminder refresh (`src/scribe_mcp/tools/set_project.py:600-686`, `:756-920`, `:1022-1149`, `:1153-1203`).
2. Council contexts add post-tool Codex hook work around Scribe calls: after `mcp__scribe__set_project`, generated `post_tool.py` writes local binding/cache/session records and attempts HookClient HTTP binding/logging (`scribe_mcp/.codex/hooks/post_tool.py:273-315`, `:318-423`; same logic in `council_mcp/.codex/hooks/post_tool.py:273-315`, `:318-423`). This is outside the Scribe tool response but can affect perceived latency.
3. `council_mcp` has a heavier active Council runtime context: ws_proxy, runtime routing, daemon state, and a local `allow_legacy_transport_fallback: true` setting, while `scribe_mcp` currently has `allow_legacy_transport_fallback: false` (`council_mcp/.council/council.yaml:270-345`, `scribe_mcp/.council/council.yaml:266-345`). This is more relevant to Council tool startup/proxy behavior than to direct Scribe calls, but it can contaminate perceived wait time when sessions interleave Council and Scribe tools.

No root cause is declared here because I did not run a sanctioned timed `set_project` call rooted at `council_mcp`; the assignment required all Scribe/Council calls to remain bound to the active project rooted at `scribe_mcp`. The next gate should collect phase timing for a controlled Council-root invocation before implementation.


