### Finding 2: Source authority says generated client configs are outputs

Both repos' `AGENTS.md` state that `AGENTS.md`, `.codex/**`, `.claude/**`, generated configs, and compiler-managed surfaces are generated outputs, not durable source authority (`scribe_mcp/AGENTS.md:3-16`, `council_mcp/AGENTS.md:3-16`). Council MCP service source says `.mcp.json` and `.codex/config.toml` are emitted by export paths (`council_mcp/src/council_mcp/services/mcp_servers.py:2582-2608`, `:2631-2653`).

### Finding 3: Direct-Scribe warning exists and no Scribe proxy tool is exposed in current config

Both generated instruction surfaces tell agents to use direct `mcp__scribe__*` tools and not substitute shell calls (`scribe_mcp/AGENTS.md:82-87`, `:153-164`; `council_mcp/AGENTS.md:82-87`, `:153-164`). The inspected Codex configs expose Scribe as its own MCP server and do not show a Council `scribe_call` proxy in `enabled_tools` (`scribe_mcp/.codex/config.toml:47-55`, `:119-124`; `council_mcp/.codex/config.toml:52-59`, `:124-129`).


